3. AeroSpace  -  https://github.com/nikitabobko/AeroSpace  (MIT, (c) 2023 Nikita Bobko)
==============================================================================

What is derived from it:

  * The rules for telling real windows from popups, and which windows float
    (`classify`, `isPopup` and `floatsByDefault` in src/model.zig), including
    its lists of applications and the cases they were found for, are ported
    from AeroSpace's `AxUiElementWindowType.swift` (isWindowHeuristic and
    isDialogHeuristic).
  * The native-tab switch detection (`isTabSwap`, and its use in src/wm.zig)
    follows AeroSpace's `nonidempotentNativeTabSwapHeuristic`.
  * The idea of treating the lock screen as a reason to pause, and of keeping a
    memory of lost windows, comes from AeroSpace's closed-windows cache.
  * Otherwise it was studied as a reference for how to manage windows on macOS
    (parking windows off-screen, finding the focused window, which
    Accessibility calls to use).

